  "raw_text": "it just tastes good. Agent: That's very descriptive. What are the top two or three things that make that Arby's brisket sandwich \"perfect\" for you? User: The way they slice it really thin and the seasoning that they use to cook with it. Agent: Okay, I understand. On the flip side, what are the top two or three things that would make that brisket sandwich \"bad\" for you? For example, if it were soggy, dry, or cold? User: If it was overcooked. Agent: Understood. What else would make it bad, besides being overcooked? User: If they put too much seasoning on it and if they slice it, could they slice it really thin? If they sliced it too thick, I think that would take away from the texture of it. Agent: Thank you for... User: don't... Agent: Thank you for clarifying. If the Arby's brisket sandwich was unavailable, what would you order instead, including the chain and the specific item? User: Probably the roast beef. Agent: And why is the roast beef the closest replacement for you? User: Beca",
